-- title:
--   Two special-fibre components of X₁(Mp) as distinct prime divisors
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $p$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb Q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j\in K$ be the element mapping to [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) in $L((q))$, assumed nonzero. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, write $X=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) for the two-chart model over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and $X_k$ for the pullback of $X$ along $\operatorname{Spec} k\to\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $c_v\colon C_v\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ ($v=1,2$) be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$, geometrically integral and integral, and let $i_v$ be morphisms $C_v\to X_k$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ (pairs consisting of a morphism whose composite with the second projection is $c_v$) which are closed immersions, such that every point of $X_k$ lies in the range of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the fibre product $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ is reduced, and its carrier has cardinality $n>0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O\colon A\to O$ carrying the maximal ideal of $A$ to the maximal ideal of $O$ (as an ideal image), let $\tau\colon O\to k$ satisfy $\tau\circ\rho_O=(A\to k)$, and let $bc\colon X_k\to X_O$ be a morphism into the pullback of $X$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\rho_O$ commuting with the projections to $X$ and compatible with $\operatorname{Spec}\tau$ on the base. Put $f_v=i_v$ followed by $bc$, let $\mathcal I_v$ be the kernel ideal sheaf of $f_v$, $\mathcal I_0$ that of $bc$, and $\xi_v=f_v(\eta_{C_v})$ the image of the generic point. Then the closed subscheme cut out by each $\mathcal I_v$ is integral; $\mathcal I_v$ is the vanishing ideal sheaf of the closed set $\overline{\{\xi_v\}}$; the set-theoretic image of $f_v$ equals $\overline{\{\xi_v\}}$; $\xi_1\notin\overline{\{\xi_2\}}$ and $\xi_2\notin\overline{\{\xi_1\}}$; $\mathcal I_0\le\mathcal I_1$, $\mathcal I_0\le\mathcal I_2$, and $\mathcal I_1\sqcap\mathcal I_2=\mathcal I_0$.
--
--   This identifies the two components of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$, after the unramified base change $A\to O$, with two distinct incomparable vertical prime divisors on $X_O$ whose ideal sheaves intersect exactly in the ideal sheaf of the closed fibre; the components are the Igusa components of Deligne–Rapoport and Katz–Mazur. It is the geometric input for the subsequent statements on invertibility of these ideal sheaves, on the factorisation of the closed-fibre ideal as a product, and on the local generation of the kernel ideals.
